.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH nut-config 1  "nut-cli 0.1.0" nut
.SH NAME
nut\-config \- Inspect, scaffold, render, or diff host settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnut config\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect, scaffold, render, or diff host settings
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color output policy
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Color when writing to a terminal (default)
.IP \(bu 2
always: Color even when piped
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never color
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII symbols and bars
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON where supported
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Include additional diagnostic detail
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read host settings from this file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
nut\-config\-path(1)
Print the selected host configuration path and why it was chosen
.TP
nut\-config\-show(1)
Parse and display the selected host configuration
.TP
nut\-config\-new(1)
Scaffold a commented host config from live USB and DMI discovery
.TP
nut\-config\-render(1)
Render NUT files and the event hook with secret placeholders
.TP
nut\-config\-diff(1)
Compare rendered files with live NUT configuration. Secrets are masked
